 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bekhorot.27b.3",
   "daf": "27b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "בְּכוֹר נֶאֱכָל שָׁנָה בְּשָׁנָה כּוּ׳. מִדְּקָאָמַר ״נוֹלַד בּוֹ מוּם בְּתוֹךְ שְׁנָתוֹ״, לְמֵימְרָא דִּלְשָׁנָה דִּידֵיהּ מָנֵינַן. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «The firstborn animal is eaten year by year,» i.e., within its first year, whether it is blemished or unblemished. The Gemara comments: «From» the fact «that» the mishna «says: If a blemish developed within its» first «year,» rather than within the first year, that is «to say that we count» according «to its year,» not by the calendar year. In other words, the year is calculated from the day of the animal’s birth. «From where is this matter» derived?"
  }
